      "spam": false,
      "statusChangeID": null,
      "value": "I’m aware that manual resizing is being considered, but this request is for an automatic solution based on real height, not a user selected percentage of original scale. Both systems could be present at one time, enabling automatic resizing disables custom scale.",
      "viewerReactions": null
    }
  ],
  "companyID": "58c62e995865713647a7115d",
  "created": "2021-04-01T20:23:00.156Z",
  "deletedAt": null,
  "details": "Might sound familiar if any of you remember Snow Crash. Basically, when a specific toggle next to the real height setting is checked, all avatars are automatically sized up or down until their viewpoint matches that chosen height in-game, based on the simple 1:1 Unitymetric = metric conversion already relied on by avatar and world creators.\nHaving access to avatars of all different shapes and sizes is great, but often, an avatar that’s far too large or much too small can make worlds and other players very difficult to interact with properly. Changing avatars is an option of course, but being able to wear whatever you want without worrying about changing size constantly would be nice.",
